{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "stitches",
  "name": "Stitches",
  "role": "Tank",
  "overview": "Stitches is a Tank whose signature move is Hook, a unique Ability that can be used to pull enemy Heroes from the distance and allow allied Heroes to follow up with crowd control and burst damage.",
  "strengths": [
    "Solid waveclear",
    "Powerful high-range pull effect",
    "High maximum Health",
    "Good self-sustain",
    "Decent damage"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Low crowd control",
    "Lack of mobility",
    "Weak peeling"
  ],
  "synergies": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "blaze",
        "name": "Blaze"
      },
      {
        "id": "falstad",
        "name": "Falstad"
      },
      {
        "id": "kaelthas",
        "name": "Kael'thas"
      },
      {
        "id": "malfurion",
        "name": "Malfurion"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Stitches works well with Heroes who can quickly respond to any successful Hook by locking the target enemy Hero in place with crowd control (for example Malfurion with Entangling Roots) and that have access to burst damage to get a kill before the enemy team can react (such as Jaina).\n\nTo compensate his lack of peeling, Stitches likes to be in team with Heroes that have access to crowd control. We recommend an Offlaner who can act as a secondary Tank during team fights (for example Blaze).\n\nIf your team has access to a disengage tool (such as Mighty Gust), they can use it either to save you from danger or to knock the rest of the enemy team away right after you Hook someone."
  },
  "counters": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "johanna",
        "name": "Johanna"
      },
      {
        "id": "malthael",
        "name": "Malthael"
      },
      {
        "id": "greymane",
        "name": "Greymane"
      },
      {
        "id": "tychus",
        "name": "Tychus"
      },
      {
        "id": "anduin",
        "name": "Anduin"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Because so much of Stitches's ability to impact a match is baked into Hook, he can be challenged by frontline Heroes who are bad targets for it as they may use Unstoppable on demand, put a Summon on the trajectory, easily dodge the skillshot, or run away right after. Heroes who can save the target right after they get caught are good counters as well.\n\nDue to his high Health pool and lack of mobility, Stitches is also susceptible to percent-based damage (for example Leoric with Drain Hope and Entomb)."
  },
